# r41n // 0xraiven.github.io

> Public offensive security portfolio, red teaming repository, and technical knowledge base maintained by
**[@0xraiven](https://github.com/0xraiven)**.

---

## Purpose & Scope

This platform serves as a centralized, open-access operational archive for:

- **Security Engineering & Tools ([`/projects`](https://0xraiven.github.io/projects))**: Open-source cybersecurity
tools, threat detection sensors, and security architectures.
- **Offensive Security Walkthroughs ([`/writeups`](https://0xraiven.github.io/writeups))**: Detailed attack paths,
Active Directory escalation vectors, and Hack The Box machine writeups categorized across Low, Medium, Hard, and Insane
tiers.
- **Tactical Field Notes ([`/notes`](https://0xraiven.github.io/notes))**: Incident runbooks, command cheatsheets, and
privilege escalation techniques.
- **Vulnerability Research ([`/research`](https://0xraiven.github.io/research))**: Threat modeling, vulnerability
analysis, and exploit research.
- **Operator Profile & Resume ([`/about`](https://0xraiven.github.io/about),
[`/resume`](https://0xraiven.github.io/resume))**: Background, technical competencies, and professional credentials.
- **Direct Dispatch & Communications ([`/contact`](https://0xraiven.github.io/contact))**: Verified public coordinates,
ProtonMail E2EE WKD routing, and direct dispatch channel.

---

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: [Next.js](https://nextjs.org/) (App Router, Static HTML Export)
- **Styling**: [Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/) v4 with custom Obsidian & Wine Red aesthetic tokens
- **CMS**: [Keystatic](https://keystatic.com/) (File-based Markdown & MDOC collections)
- **Icons**: [Lucide React](https://lucide.dev/)
- **Deployment**: [GitHub Pages](https://pages.github.com/) via GitHub Actions CI/CD

---

## 💻 Local Development

```bash
# Install dependencies
npm install

# Run repo sync and local dev server
npm run dev

# Build static production bundle
npm run build
```